# Vulcan foundations

Sibling bar to Argus. These rules apply to every phase — do not re-litigate them in chat.

## Contract-first serving

- Every serving backend under `serving/*` MUST implement `contracts/model-contract` exactly: `GET /health`, `GET /metrics`, `POST /v1/infer`, `GET /v1/resources` (+ static resource-requirements manifest).
- Do not expose per-backend native APIs as the north-bound platform surface. Adapters wrap natives; the OpenAPI/JSON Schema contract is the API ([ADR-001](docs/adr/001-unified-model-serving-contract.md)).
- Contract changes update OpenAPI + JSON Schema + tests together.

## CPU-fallback mandatory (no GPU spend in CI)

- CI **never** provisions or runs against real GPU hardware or cloud GPU nodes ([ADR-002](docs/adr/002-gpu-cost-safety-policy.md)).
- Every serving backend MUST have a CPU-only dev mode against a small reference model (`cpu_dev_mode: true`).
- GPU infra under `gpu-infra/` and `infra/` is **validated** in CI (`terraform validate|plan`, `helm template` + kubeconform, conftest/OPA) but **never applied** by automation.
- Real GPU benchmarks are manual only — document under `docs/benchmarks/`.

## ADR discipline

- Meaningful architectural choices get an ADR in `docs/adr/` before or with the implementing PR.
- Changes under `contracts/` or `gpu-infra/` without a corresponding ADR update fail CI (ADR presence gate).
- Link new ADRs from `docs/adr/index.md` and the root README when user-facing.

## Commit messages (standing)

Every commit MUST use exactly one of these forms — no ad hoc subjects:

```text
phase-N: <summary>
fix(<component>): <summary>
```

- **`phase-N:`** — phase deliverables (e.g. `phase-4: Triton adapter.`).
- **`fix(<component>):`** — out-of-band fixes outside a phase bump (e.g. `fix(triton): wait for health before conformance`).

Do **not** use messages like `start triton serving` or `make changes to the benchmark results`. This is a standing rule going forward; do not rewrite existing history to retrofit it.

Prefer small PRs mapped to a single phase or component.

## Git discipline

- Commit only when asked (or when the phase Definition of Done explicitly requires commit/push).
- Never update git config; never `--no-verify` / skip hooks unless explicitly requested.
- Never force-push `main`/`master`; never destructive resets unless explicitly requested.
- Do not amend commits you did not create in this session, or commits already pushed, unless the user explicitly asks and amend rules are met.

## Coverage gate

- Gated packages must keep **≥ 65%** coverage in CI (`COVERAGE_MIN=65`), same bar as Argus.
- New libraries/services add unit tests before claiming done; do not lower the gate.

## Layout

- Contracts in `contracts/`; serving adapters in `serving/{common,bentoml,ray-serve,triton,vllm,kserve}/`.
- GPU orchestration in `gpu-infra/` and `autoscaling/`; cloud packaging in `infra/{terraform,helm,argocd}/`.
- Docs and ADRs in `docs/`; do not invent parallel top-level doc trees.
- Every component ships a `README.md`.

## Port allocation (host)

- **Vulcan owns host ports `9000–9099`.** Do not bind Vulcan services outside this range.
- Rationale: sibling stacks (e.g. Argus on 3000/808x/809x) often share a laptop; colliding ports break local compose.
- Reserved map (extend in compose comments as services land):
  - `9000` — `serving/bentoml`
  - `9001` — `serving/common` reference server
  - `9002` — `serving/ray-serve`
  - `9003` — `serving/triton` (contract shim; Triton engine stays internal)
  - `9004` — `serving/vllm` (contract shim; vLLM/OpenAI engine stays internal)
  - `9005` — optional local `kubectl port-forward` for KServe (no compose service)
  - `9006` — `bedrock-gateway` optional local shim (no compose; mocked in CI)
  - `9007` — `gateway` (routing; ADR-006)
  - `9008–9098` — future backends / observability
  - Phase 6–9 K8s/GPU infra + phase 10 SageMaker: **no** docker-compose host port (validate-only / moto in CI)
  - `9099` — optional contract-stub / docs static
- Reference server, stubs, and compose `ports:` MUST use this range. Never default to `8080`/`8090`/etc.

## Secrets & local stack

- Never commit secrets; use `.env.example`.
- Default `make up` is CPU-only via `docker-compose.yml`.
